  "nl_text": "The rschema_0098 database is designed to manage information about users, employees, technical solutions, and their evaluations and feedback. At the core of this database is the User table, which stores details about individual users, including their email, gender, name, phone number, and a unique User ID. The Employee table contains similar information about employees, such as their contact number, email, name, and gender, with a unique Employee ID. The Technical_solution table stores details about the technical solutions implemented, including the implementation start and end dates, a description, name, and status, with a unique Technical_solution ID. The Technical_solution_feedback table captures feedback from users about the technical solutions, including the feedback content, date, satisfaction level, and any user suggestions, with a composite primary key consisting of the User ID, Technical_solution ID, and feedback date. This table also includes foreign keys referencing the User and Technical_solution tables to establish relationships between users and the solutions they provide feedback on. The Technical_solution_evaluation table stores evaluations of the technical solutions by employees, including the evaluation content, date, indicators, and results, with a composite primary key consisting of the Technical_solution ID, Employee ID, and evaluation date. This table also includes foreign keys referencing the Employee and Technical_solution tables to establish relationships between employees and the solutions they evaluate.",
  "gold_question": "In modern enterprises, the management and evaluation of technology solutions is an important part of ensuring that technology investment generates maximum value and promotes business innovation. With the rapid development of information technology, various technology solutions (such as software tools, hardware equipment, cloud services, artificial intelligence systems, etc.) have become key means for enterprises to improve efficiency, reduce costs, and optimize products and services. However, how to effectively manage and evaluate these technology solutions to ensure that they meet business needs and achieve expected results has become a challenge for enterprises.\nTherefore, enterprises need a dedicated technology solution management and evaluation system. Management of technology solutions: record and track the selection, implementation and maintenance process of various technology solutions to ensure that they can continue to meet the technology needs of the enterprise.\nEvaluation of solutions: evaluate the effectiveness of various technology solutions, evaluate their cost-effectiveness, implementation progress, user feedback, etc.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0098.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0098\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `technical_solution` (\n  `technical_solution_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text NOT NULL,\n  `implementation_start_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `implementation_end_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`technical_solution_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `technical_solution_feedback` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `technical_solution_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `feedback_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `feedback_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `satisfaction_level` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_suggestions` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `technical_solution_id`, `feedback_date`),\n  CONSTRAINT `technical_solution_feedback_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `technical_solution_feedback_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`technical_solution_id`) REFERENCES `technical_solution` (`technical_solution_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `technical_solution_evaluation` (\n  `technical_solution_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `evaluation_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `evaluation_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `indicators` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `results` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`technical_solution_id`, `employee_id`, `evaluation_date`),\n  CONSTRAINT `technical_solution_evaluation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`technical_solution_id`) REFERENCES `technical_solution` (`technical_solution_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `technical_solution_evaluation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
